# Template for the gitignored `.env`. Copy it and fill in your own values:
#
#     cp .env.template .env
#
# Everything here is personal: each contributor uses their own DagsHub account
# and their own token, so a leaked or revoked token costs one person a minute,
# not the team a migration. `.env` is in `.gitignore` and stays there.
#
# `recommenditos/config.py` loads `.env` with python-dotenv at import time, so
# every pipeline stage, every test and every script sees these values without
# doing anything itself.
#
# Full walkthrough from a fresh clone to a pulled dataset and a visible MLflow
# run: docs/docs/getting-started.md.

# --- DagsHub ----------------------------------------------------------------
# One DagsHub repository is both our DVC remote and our MLflow tracking server:
# https://dagshub.com/recommenditos/MLOPS_Recommenditos (EDN-19).
#
# Where to get the token: sign in to DagsHub, open your avatar in the top right
# -> "Your Settings" -> "Tokens", and copy the "Default Access Token" (or create
# a new one). It is a password: it is not shown again after you leave the page on
# a freshly created token, and it grants everything your account can do.

# Your DagsHub login name, not your e-mail address.
DAGSHUB_USERNAME=
# The access token from the page above.
DAGSHUB_USER_TOKEN=

# --- MLflow -----------------------------------------------------------------
# MLflow reads these three names from the environment itself, which is why the
# same token appears twice on purpose: DagsHub's tracking server authenticates
# with HTTP basic auth and takes the token as the password. Nothing converts one
# pair into the other, so both have to be filled in.
# `recommenditos/tracking.py` checks all three before a run starts.

# The `.mlflow` endpoint of the repository above. The same for everyone.
MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=https://dagshub.com/recommenditos/MLOPS_Recommenditos.mlflow
# The same value as DAGSHUB_USERNAME.
MLFLOW_TRACKING_USERNAME=
# The same value as DAGSHUB_USER_TOKEN.
MLFLOW_TRACKING_PASSWORD=
